      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/7feea3/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-02-11T23:51:04.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Put 1 token in the hero favor pool when any of these things occur: A hero target deals 2 or more damage to multiple non-hero targets in a single round</p><p>Put 1 token in the Bloodsworn favor pool when any of these things occur: A villain target deals 2 or more damage to multiple non-villain targets in a single round</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>First, I suppose a round is a complete sequence of turns: from the villain turn to the environment turn, through the heroes' turns</p><p>Is the favor awarded once per every target earning it or once per instance of multiple damage happening (even coming from the same target multiple times) or even once per game round per side?</p><p>Example: three heroes game, hero A manages to damage 2 villain targets for 2 damage each during his turn. Hero B manages to damage 2 targets for 2 each with a card and do it again with a power, all during her turn. Hero C doesn't deal damage at all.</p><p>How many total favor tokens did the heroes earn? 2, 3 or 1? Obviously not considering titles awarded or targets destroyed</p><p>Also, when is it approriate to award thoe tokens? As soon as the condition for awarding them is fulfilled? I ask because if it was \"once per game round stop\" it would make sense if the condition was only checked at the end of the round</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:43:43.156Z",
